hook.extract_worker.output_json_array_co:
Output a JSON array: [{"content": "concise fact, at most 150 characters", "type": "factual|procedural|architectural|pitfall|decision"}]

Examples (worth extracting):
  {"content": "ripgrep skips files listed in .gitignore and hidden files by default; add --no-ignore --hidden to search everything", "type": "factual"}
  {"content": "On an entry-level GPU, qwen3:1.7b generate takes about 30s and qwen3-embedding embed about 5s", "type": "factual"}
  {"content": "LanceDB search uses the cosine metric; below min_score 0.65 is mostly noise", "type": "architectural"}

Examples (do not extract):
  ✗ "Python dict is a hash table" -> general knowledge
  ✗ "Edited line 43 of config.py" -> session progress, not knowledge
  ✗ "Use git commit to commit changes" -> common sense

