hook.post_tool_use.aec_pending:
[Guardian:AEC-Pending] (d)/(h) has {count} item(s) that push memory writes to later:
{items}
If worth writing, atom_write it now, then call anti_evasion_report again and change that item to "→ written to atom <name>" (or "→ not writing (reason)"); otherwise Stop will block.

hook.pre_tool_use_svn.test_block:
[Guardian:SvnTestBlock] The paths of this svn commit include test files or test directories: {paths}. This project is configured not to put test / practice files into svn (svn_test_block in overview-hub.json).
- If you did not mean to commit tests -> remove these paths from the commit path list and commit again;
- If the user said this turn that tests should go into svn as well -> add a line `{quote_line}` at the start of this command; if the quote is in this turn's user words and not negated, it is let through and logged;
- If unsure -> ask the user first.

hook.release_rules.fix_escalation:
[Guardian:FixEscalation] Repeated fix attempts detected (retry={count}).
{rounds}
Per the "precise fix escalation" rule, stop and fix directly: write three sentences covering (1) the failure symptom and its original text, (2) the fixes already tried and why each did not work, (3) the smallest next check that can tell the candidate causes apart; do that check before touching code again. Deliberate red runs (reverting to old code as counter-proof) do not count.

hook.stop.aec_pending:
[Guardian:AEC-Pending] The closing check puts off {count} memory write(s):
{items}
That leaves the knowledge to the next turn (the user would have to ask again before it gets filled in), which breaks the anti-evasion contract. Finish the atom_write now, then call anti_evasion_report again and change each item to "→ written to atom <name>" (or "→ not written (one-line reason)"); (h) lists only what the user has to do.

hook.verify_batch.deny_with_fix:
{tag} {line}
{fix}
To turn this gate off: workflow/config.json guard.verify_batch.enabled=false.

hook.wg_core.guardian_atomfunnelblock_wr:
[Guardian:AtomFunnelBlock] Writing or editing an atom .md directly, bypassing the funnel, is forbidden.
Path: {fp_str}
Correct approach:
  (1) Use the MCP tools `atom_write` / `atom_promote` / `atom_move`;
      to change only Trigger/Related/Tags metadata -> `atom_edit_meta` (surgical edit, byte-stable)
  (2) In code: write knowledge content with lib.atom_io.write_atom() / write_raw() / edit_metadata();
      write counter fields (read_hits / last_used / confirmations) with lib.atom_access
Emergency bypass: set the environment variable `WG_DISABLE_ATOM_GUARD=1` and retry.

hook.wg_core.guardian_crossrealmbashbloc:
[Guardian:CrossRealmBashBlock] A project session must not modify the ~/.claude core layer (hooks/lib/tools/skills/rules/prompts, root-level settings and docs) or operate the root repo (git add/commit/push) via Bash/PowerShell.
Command: {cmd}
session cwd: {cwd}
Rule hit: {rule}: {why} | evidence: {evidence}
Rule: when a project layer needs a root-layer change -> do not act; write the need as a pasteable prompt for the user and ask them to run it in a ~/.claude session (that is where verify runs, selective staging and push happen).
Project's own needs -> write <project-root>/.claude/hooks/project_hooks.py or .claude/skills/.
If you only need to run a root-layer tool (read-only, or aimed at this project) -> do not cd into ~/.claude; run `python "<memory-system folder>/tools/<tool>.py" ...` by its absolute path directly.
